        "rephrase": {
          "p_ql3": "Reported evaluation limits: accuracy on completed answers barely moved (50% vs 52%), tracing out-of-memory errors to multiple models in one runtime, not the KV cache.",
          "p_ql1": "Trained 0.52% of Llama 3.1 8B parameters with QLoRA (4-bit, Unsloth, TRL) on a free 15 GB GPU, raising answer completion from 32% to 52% and exact-answer accuracy from 16.2% to 27.3% (n=99)."
        },
        "profile": "Builds the modelling a brief needs and reports its limits plainly: gradient boosting (XGBoost churn), LSTM time-series forecasting with time-ordered validation, text clustering (SBERT, K-Means, DBSCAN) and 11,459 per-gene models (train Pearson 0.807 vs test 0.545). Works with clients: scoped a loosely defined brief at 180 Degrees Consulting into a stakeholder demo (5-star rating) and contributed to the client's production MCP server, now in live use. Deploys on AWS and GCP (Lambda, Cloud Run) with CI/CD and MLflow experiment tracking. Builds deployable ML models: forecasting (an LSTM time-series service), propensity modelling (an XGBoost churn classifier with Bayesian tuning and SMOTE) and customer segmentation (k-means, HAC and DBSCAN)."
      },
